<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Novara (1513)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1513">1513</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-league-of-cambrai">War of the League of Cambrai</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Novara was fought on 6 June 1513 near Novara in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, when a Swiss army defending Duke Massimiliano Sforza of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> made a surprise attack on the French army under Louis de La Trémoille and routed it. The victory marked the height of Swiss military power and expelled the French from the Duchy of Milan, until their return two years later at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-marignano">Marignano</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-novara-1513.jpg" alt="Battle of Novara (1513)" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johannes Stumpf · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schlacht_bei_Novara_1513.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
